---
description: TaskHub DevOps & Tools Best Practices
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use PNPM workspaces for dependency management; always install from root.
- Use workspace:* protocol for internal dependencies.
- Run scripts with `--filter` or `-r` as appropriate.
- CI/CD: Use GitHub Actions, with separate jobs for frontend and backend, and dependency caching.
- Use Docker Compose for local development with hot-reloading.
- All new features must have tests (Vitest for frontend, xUnit for backend).
- Lint and format code with ESLint and Prettier; enforce via pre-commit hooks and CI.
- Use Serilog for backend logging, Sentry for error tracking, and Application Insights for performance.
- Use Dependabot/Renovate for dependency scanning; never commit secrets.
- Document APIs with Swagger/OpenAPI and maintain a root README.
- All changes require code review before merging.